Chapter: SmpApPortIo

 A device port read taken on an APPLICATION PROCESSOR must answer what the
 same read answers on the boot processor. It did not: codex-vm served COM1
 to an AP and returned 0 for every other port, so a process claimed by an AP
 read the NE2000's CR, ISR and BNRY as 0, 0, 0 where proc 0 read 2, 0, 70,
 and a service that had to reach a device could only be run pinned to core 0
 (plugs-backlog 2.45, L-ARENA: the bed was less capable than the board in
 exactly the respect under test).

 THE ARM COMPARES THE TWO PROCESSORS RATHER THAN ASSERTING CONSTANTS, because
 the register values depend on how far NIC bring-up has got and an arm that
 named 2, 0, 70 would go red on a change to the driver rather than to the bed.
 What must hold is that the answer does not depend on which processor asked.
 It also prints whether the boot processor's own read is non-zero, so a run
 where BOTH answer 0 -- no NIC on the bus, nothing to read -- is visible as
 the vacuous pass it would otherwise be (L-VACUOUS).

Section: Body

 CR is base+0, BNRY base+3 and ISR base+7 on the NE2000 at 0x300.

  ne2k-cr : Integer = 768
  ne2k-bnry : Integer = 771
  ne2k-isr : Integer = 775

  read-triple : Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  read-triple (base) = act
    cr <- port-in-byte ne2k-cr
    bnry <- port-in-byte ne2k-bnry
    isr <- port-in-byte ne2k-isr
    let a = atomic-store base cr
    in let b = atomic-store (base + 8) bnry
    in let c = atomic-store (base + 16) isr
    in cr + bnry + isr
  end

  child-body : Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  child-body (x) = read-triple 36240

  opening : [Console, Concurrent, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    bsp <- read-triple 36264
    a <- process-spawn-on-core (\x -> child-body x) 2
    wa <- process-wait a
    let bcr = atomic-load 36264
    in let bbn = atomic-load 36272
    in let bis = atomic-load 36280
    in let acr = atomic-load 36240
    in let abn = atomic-load 36248
    in let ais = atomic-load 36256
    in let same = if acr == bcr then if abn == bbn then ais == bis else False else False
    in act
      print-line-uni ("bsp read something " & show (bcr + bbn + bis > 0))
      print-line-uni (if same then "ap agrees with bsp" else "AP DISAGREES WITH BSP")
    end
  end
